    "name": "Twenty CRM Companies People API",
    "schema": "https://schema.getpostman.com/json/collection/v2.1.0/collection.json",
    "description": {
      "content": "REST specification for Twenty, the open-source CRM. Twenty auto-generates a REST API (and a parallel GraphQL API) from your workspace data model. This document covers the Core API (CRUD over records such as People, Companies, Opportunities, Notes, and Tasks) and the Metadata API (schema management for objects and fields). Endpoints are served from a per-workspace base URL: https://api.twenty.com on Twenty Cloud, or https://{your-domain} when self-hosted. The Core API lives under /rest and the Metadata API under /rest/metadata. All requests are authenticated with a Bearer API key created in Settings -> API & Webhooks.\n\nContact Support:\n Name: Twenty",
      "type": "text/plain"
    }
  }
